{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016eyv9vkX1SKg75iGrpyTAf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Defer Round 0 D2H Synchronization\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tRestructure the Round 0 per-AIR loop in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` to eliminate blocking D2H synchronization points between GPU kernel launches. Currently, each of the ~1,246 kernel results (2 per AIR instance) triggers a `to_host()` call that blocks the CPU via `cudaEventSynchronize`, creating pipeline stalls. By deferring all D2H transfers to after all kernels are queued, the GPU executes kernels back-to-back without host-side stalls.\n6\t\n7\tThis targets Round 0, the single largest contributor to the GPU prover's failure to scale with APC count: Round 0 *increases* from 178ms to 663ms (+485ms, 3.7x) as APCs go from 0 to 300, despite total work (cells, constraints, bus interaction messages) all decreasing by >2x.\n8\t\n9\t## Current Code Path\n10\t\n11\t### Call Chain\n12\t\n13\t1. `logup_zerocheck_prove` (mod.rs:224) calls `prover.sumcheck_uni_round0_polys(ctx, lambda)`\n14\t2. `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (mod.rs:598-884):\n15\t   - Lines 600-728: Setup (lambda powers, eq precomputation, selectors, etc.)\n16\t   - Lines 730-880: **The per-AIR loop** (this is what we modify)\n17\t   - Lines 881-883: Emit metrics, return `batch_sp_poly`\n18\t\n19\t### The Per-AIR Loop (lines 730-880)\n20\t\n21\tFor each AIR instance (`trace_idx` from 0 to `num_present_airs - 1`):\n22\t\n23\t1. **Setup** (lines 742-771): Compute `single_pk`, `single_air_constraints`, `local_constraint_deg`, `omega_root`, build `d_main_parts` (device buffer of device pointers to trace matrices), look up `eq_xi_tree`.\n24\t\n25\t2. **Zerocheck kernel launch + sync** (lines 777-827):\n26\t   - `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(...)` → returns `DeviceBuffer<EF>` (result on GPU)\n27\t   - `sum_buffer.to_host()` at line 792 — **BLOCKING SYNC** via `cudaEventSynchronize`\n28\t   - CPU IDFT: transpose to row-major, call `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft`\n29\t   - Polynomial construction: multiply by `(Z^{2^l_skip} - 1)`, debug assert sum = 0\n30\t   - Store result in `batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx]`\n31\t\n32\t3. **Logup kernel launch + sync** (lines 831-879):\n33\t   - `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu(...)` → returns `DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` (result on GPU)\n34\t   - `sum.to_host()` at line 848 — **BLOCKING SYNC** via `cudaEventSynchronize`\n35\t   - Unzip into numer/denom, optional normalization for negative `n`\n36\t   - Transpose to row-major, call `from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft` twice (numer + denom)\n37\t   - Store results in `batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx]` and `batch_sp_poly[2 * trace_idx + 1]`\n38\t\n39\t### Why It's Slow\n40\t\n41\tEach `to_host()` call (copy.rs:102-125) does:\n42\t1. `cudaMemcpyAsync(D2H, cudaStreamPerThread)` — queue async copy\n43\t2. `COPY_EVENT.record_and_wait(cudaStreamPerThread)` — record event then `cudaEventSynchronize` (CPU blocks until ALL prior stream work completes)\n44\t\n45\tThis means the CPU blocks after every single kernel, waiting for the GPU. Since kernels are tiny (each processes one AIR's constraints for a few cosets), the GPU is idle during CPU processing time, and the CPU is idle during GPU kernel execution. With 623 AIR instances at APC 300, there are 1,246 such blocking sync points.\n46\t\n47\t### Key Properties\n48\t\n49\t- **All loop iterations are independent**: zerocheck/logup for AIR[i] reads only from AIR[i]'s trace, selectors, and proving key. The shared read-only inputs (`d_lambda_pows`, `eq_xi_tree`, `beta_pows`) are immutable.\n50\t- **Result buffers are tiny**: `DeviceBuffer<EF>` holds `num_cosets_zc * skip_domain` elements (~4-16 EF values); `DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` holds `num_cosets_logup * skip_domain` (~4-16 Frac values). Each is < 1KB.\n51\t- **`d_main_parts` is per-iteration**: Created at line 768 from device pointers into `air_ctx` trace matrices. The trace matrices themselves are owned by `ProvingContext` and live throughout. `d_main_parts` is just an index array of device pointers.\n52\t- **Temporary buffers inside kernel functions are stream-ordered freed**: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` create large temporary buffers (`intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`) that are dropped when the function returns. This is safe because `DeviceBuffer::drop` calls `cudaFreeAsync` (stream-ordered) — the GPU will finish reading the buffer before the free executes. This remains safe in the deferred approach because all operations are on the same `cudaStreamPerThread`.\n53\t- **Memory allocation is also stream-ordered**: `d_malloc` uses `cudaMallocAsync` for small buffers and VPMM for large ones. Both are ordered with respect to `cudaStreamPerThread`, so new allocations can reuse memory from prior stream-ordered frees.\n54\t\n55\t## Changes\n56\t\n57\t### Overview\n58\t\n59\tSplit the single per-AIR loop (lines 730-880) into two phases:\n60\t- **Phase 1** (GPU launch): Iterate all AIRs, launch kernels, collect GPU result buffers\n61\t- **Phase 2** (CPU processing): Transfer results D2H, perform IDFT and polynomial construction\n62\t\n63\t### Step 1: Define a per-AIR metadata struct\n64\t\n65\tAdd a local struct inside `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (or just use tuples) to hold the data needed for Phase 2 processing:\n66\t\n67\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, inside `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n68\t\n69\t```rust\n70\t// Metadata stored per AIR during Phase 1, consumed in Phase 2\n71\tstruct Round0Pending {\n72\t    trace_idx: usize,\n73\t    air_idx: usize,  // for debug assert only\n74\t    num_cosets_zc: usize,\n75\t    num_cosets_logup: usize,\n76\t    local_constraint_deg: usize,\n77\t    omega_root: F,\n78\t    n: i32,  // n_per_trace value, for normalization check\n79\t    zc_result: DeviceBuffer<EF>,       // may be empty\n80\t    logup_result: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,  // may be empty\n81\t}\n82\t```\n83\t\n84\t### Step 2: Phase 1 — GPU launch loop\n85\t\n86\tReplace lines 730-880 with a Phase 1 loop that launches kernels without D2H transfers.\n87\t\n88\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n89\t\n90\tThe new Phase 1 loop:\n91\t```rust\n92\tlet mut pending: Vec<Round0Pending> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n93\t// Collect d_main_parts to keep them alive until all kernels complete.\n94\t// Although cudaFreeAsync is stream-ordered (so dropping would be safe),\n95\t// we retain them defensively to avoid coupling correctness to VPMM behavior.\n96\tlet mut d_main_parts_vec: Vec<DeviceBuffer<*const F>> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n97\t\n98\tfor (trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, selectors_cube, public_values, eq_3bs)) in izip!(\n99\t    &ctx.per_trace,\n100\t    &self.n_per_trace,\n101\t    &selectors_base,\n102\t    &self.public_values_per_trace,\n103\t    &self.eq_3b_per_trace,\n104\t)\n105\t.enumerate()\n106\t{\n107\t    // --- same setup as current code (lines 741-771) ---\n108\t    let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n109\t    let single_air_constraints = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n110\t    let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n111\t    // ... assert, log_large_domain, omega_root, d_main_parts setup ...\n112\t\n113\t    let d_main_parts = main_parts.to_device()?;\n114\t\n115\t    let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n116\t    let zc_result = evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(\n117\t        single_pk, selectors_cube.buffer(), &d_main_parts,\n118\t        public_values, eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift), d_lambda_pows,\n119\t        1 << l_skip, 1 << n_lift, height as u32, num_cosets_zc as u32,\n120\t        omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n121\t    )?;\n122\t\n123\t    let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n124\t    let logup_result = evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu(\n125\t        single_pk, &single_air_constraints, selectors_cube.buffer(),\n126\t        &d_main_parts, public_values, eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n127\t        &self.beta_pows, eq_3bs,\n128\t        1 << l_skip, 1 << n_lift, height as u32, num_cosets_logup as u32,\n129\t        omega_root, max_temp_bytes,\n130\t    )?;\n131\t\n132\t    d_main_parts_vec.push(d_main_parts);\n133\t    pending.push(Round0Pending {\n134\t        trace_idx,\n135\t        air_idx: *air_idx,\n136\t        num_cosets_zc,\n137\t        num_cosets_logup,\n138\t        local_constraint_deg,\n139\t        omega_root,\n140\t        n,\n141\t        zc_result,\n142\t        logup_result,\n143\t    });\n144\t}\n145\t```\n146\t\n147\tKey differences from current code:\n148\t- No `to_host()` calls — kernel results stay on GPU\n149\t- `d_main_parts` collected into `d_main_parts_vec` instead of being dropped each iteration\n150\t- Per-AIR metadata (coset counts, omega_root, n) stored in `pending` for Phase 2\n151\t\n152\t### Step 3: Phase 2 — D2H transfers and CPU processing\n153\t\n154\tAfter Phase 1, process all results. The first `to_host()` implicitly synchronizes the entire stream (waiting for all 1,246 queued kernels to complete), and subsequent calls return instantly since their data is already computed.\n155\t\n156\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n157\t\n158\t```rust\n159\t// Phase 2: D2H transfer and CPU polynomial construction\n160\tfor entry in pending {\n161\t    // Zerocheck processing (same as current lines 791-827)\n162\t    if !entry.zc_result.is_empty() {\n163\t        let q_evals = entry.zc_result.to_host()?;\n164\t        let q = {\n165\t            let mut values = EF::zero_vec(entry.num_cosets_zc << l_skip);\n166\t            for coset_idx in 0..entry.num_cosets_zc {\n167\t                for i in 0..1 << l_skip {\n168\t                    values[i * entry.num_cosets_zc + coset_idx] =\n169\t                        q_evals[(coset_idx << l_skip) + i];\n170\t                }\n171\t            }\n172\t            UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n173\t                RowMajorMatrix::new(values, entry.num_cosets_zc),\n174\t                entry.omega_root,\n175\t                entry.omega_root,\n176\t            )\n177\t        };\n178\t        let sp_0_deg = sumcheck_round0_deg(l_skip, entry.local_constraint_deg);\n179\t        let coeffs = (0..=sp_0_deg)\n180\t            .map(|i| {\n181\t                let mut c = -*q.coeffs().get(i).unwrap_or(&EF::ZERO);\n182\t                if i >= 1 << l_skip {\n183\t                    c += q.coeffs()[i - (1 << l_skip)];\n184\t                }\n185\t                c\n186\t            })\n187\t            .collect_vec();\n188\t        debug_assert_eq!(\n189\t            coeffs.iter().step_by(1 << l_skip).copied().sum::<EF>(),\n190\t            EF::ZERO,\n191\t            \"Zerocheck sum is not zero for air_id: {}\",\n192\t            entry.air_idx\n193\t        );\n194\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * num_present_airs + entry.trace_idx] = UnivariatePoly::new(coeffs);\n195\t    }\n196\t\n197\t    // Logup processing (same as current lines 847-879)\n198\t    if !entry.logup_result.is_empty() {\n199\t        let evals = entry.logup_result.to_host()?;\n200\t        let (mut numer, denom): (Vec<EF>, Vec<EF>) =\n201\t            evals.into_iter().map(|frac| (frac.p, frac.q)).unzip();\n202\t        if entry.n.is_negative() {\n203\t            let norm_factor = F::from_u32(1 << entry.n.unsigned_abs()).inverse();\n204\t            for s in &mut numer {\n205\t                *s *= norm_factor;\n206\t            }\n207\t        }\n208\t        let mut numer_values = EF::zero_vec(entry.num_cosets_logup << l_skip);\n209\t        let mut denom_values = EF::zero_vec(entry.num_cosets_logup << l_skip);\n210\t        for coset_idx in 0..entry.num_cosets_logup {\n211\t            for i in 0..1 << l_skip {\n212\t                let src = (coset_idx << l_skip) + i;\n213\t                let dst = i * entry.num_cosets_logup + coset_idx;\n214\t                numer_values[dst] = numer[src];\n215\t                denom_values[dst] = denom[src];\n216\t            }\n217\t        }\n218\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * entry.trace_idx] = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n219\t            RowMajorMatrix::new(numer_values, entry.num_cosets_logup),\n220\t            entry.omega_root,\n221\t            F::ONE,\n222\t        );\n223\t        batch_sp_poly[2 * entry.trace_idx + 1] = UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft(\n224\t            RowMajorMatrix::new(denom_values, entry.num_cosets_logup),\n225\t            entry.omega_root,\n226\t            F::ONE,\n227\t        );\n228\t    }\n229\t}\n230\t\n231\t// d_main_parts_vec dropped here — stream-ordered frees execute after all kernels have completed\n232\tdrop(d_main_parts_vec);\n233\t```\n234\t\n235\t### Step 4: Preserve debug logging\n236\t\n237\tThe current loop has `debug!(\"starting batch constraints for air_idx=...\")` at line 741. Keep this in Phase 1. No additional logging changes needed.\n238\t\n239\t### Summary of touched code\n240\t\n241\t| File | What changes |\n242\t|---|---|\n243\t| `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:730-880` | Split single per-AIR loop into Phase 1 (launch) and Phase 2 (D2H + CPU) |\n244\t\n245\tNo other files are modified. No CUDA kernel changes. No FFI changes. No new crate dependencies.\n246\t\n247\t## Invariants\n248\t\n249\t1. **Output equivalence**: `batch_sp_poly` must contain exactly the same polynomials as before. Each `batch_sp_poly[k]` is written at most once, using the same index formula. The IDFT input data and polynomial construction logic are unchanged.\n250\t\n251\t2. **Stream ordering**: All kernels and D2H transfers use `cudaStreamPerThread`. Kernels execute in the same order as before (trace_idx 0, 1, 2, ...). D2H transfers now happen after all kernels instead of interleaved, but this doesn't affect correctness since each AIR's result buffer is