{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01377Nm1tnZW5diT3pq9Wq7d","type":"tool_result","content":"74:Optionally, the CPU processing in Phase 2 can be parallelized using rayon (`par_iter`) since each AIR's IDFT is independent, further reducing CPU-side time.\n80:  - Optionally parallelizing CPU IDFTs with rayon saves additional ~50-100ms\n102:4. **Parallelize CPU IDFT with rayon** (ranked #5 standalone, but can be combined with #1): Wrap the CPU-side IDFT processing in `rayon::par_iter`. Simple and effective (~50-100ms savings) but smaller standalone impact. Included as an optional enhancement in the proposed approach."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A4bJ2faf2icpueuGAwcM3V","session_id":"ebef63bf-f161-4614-a323-d6b5d42117d0","uuid":"812c1d8d-17f9-48f8-ae39-b34d982472f4","timestamp":"2026-04-10T17:48:18.126Z"}
